{"seq":17,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-installer-open-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T12:38:41.060Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"8ffe653990033d03fac79cd462ca7c09d1d023e8c28a671b0d530056900c34c0","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes in the shared drive. Only two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments at gatehouse kiosk check-in. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the 04:00 shift on 5 Oct got through the gate fine. The note also has an action item to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nMoss's other two North notes on QFL (the 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal check-in) don't mention any ticket numbers. The Central notes list #4409 and #4412, but those are for Pree's dealer account, not QFL.\n\nOne thing to check before #4419 goes into the weekly notes: Marcus's \"Q2 expansion wrap\" note from 14 Jul 2025 also lists #4419 on QFL, but there it's *Gate 3 printer lag* (BOL printout delay), not the Door 14 scanners. One of the two descriptions may be wrong, so it's worth checking the ticket itself."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
